# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings, regardless of
# the cloning machine's OS or core.autocrlf setting — a CRLF shebang line
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`) fails with "bad interpreter" on Linux, and CRLF
# inside heredocs/quoted strings silently corrupts generated config files
# (systemd units, nginx config, .env). install.sh runs as root on a Linux
# server, so this is not optional.
*.sh text eol=lf
